  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo>,</mo></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> is real matrix of order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn></math> such that the relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> holds. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>λ</mi></math> is a real number such that the relation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>X</mi></math> holds for some non-zero real matrix <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>X</mi></math> of order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the sum of squares of all possible values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>λ</mi></math> is equal to:",
    "image": null
  },
